WEBVTT

00:00:04.030 --> 00:00:08.110
On everyone's behalf, I, Shirojiro Bertoni,

00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:10.320
Musashi Ariadust Academy's treasurer,

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:13.280
offer a toast to the spring festival preparations that begin in two days,

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:16.040
to the good will our two countries will demonstrate at said festival,

00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:18.920
and to my prosperity and the money that will fatten my wallet!

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:20.330
Cheers!

00:00:20.630 --> 00:00:21.790
Cheers!

00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:25.000
Let's begin! The meat BBQ that someone else is paying for!

00:02:06.940 --> 00:02:09.650
Now then, I've gobbled up all of the vegetables,

00:02:09.650 --> 00:02:12.320
so now we can eat as much meat as we want!

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:14.200
<i>She truly is a wolf...</i>

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:15.570
Hey!

00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:18.240
Heidi said this is all for Nate.

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:28.000
Do you really love meat that much?

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:31.260
It's in a Therianthrope's nature to—

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:32.550
Horizon?!

00:02:32.550 --> 00:02:35.430
Go on. Open your mouth and go "Ah!"

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:36.760
But...

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:38.140
"Ah!"

00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:39.600
Come on. "Ah!"

00:02:56.410 --> 00:02:58.450
<i>What's with this turn of events?</i>

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:07.630
This has been puzzling me for a while now,

00:03:07.630 --> 00:03:10.800
but how are you able to eat with that scarf on?

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:12.460
It's a ninjutsu.

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:13.590
Tenzo!

00:03:13.590 --> 00:03:14.420
Beer!

00:03:14.420 --> 00:03:15.130
Judge!

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:23.020
You're a hardworking person, aren't you?

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:23.600
Huh?

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:25.600
Isn't it tough?

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:28.730
You're always running about doing the bidding of others.

00:03:28.730 --> 00:03:32.480
Judge. Doing so sits well with me.

00:03:32.480 --> 00:03:35.400
But isn't it filled with hardship?

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:38.280
There must be times when you have to do something you don't want to...

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:42.200
Ninja must hide their feelings as they carry out their duties.

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:44.330
But! Even so—

00:03:44.330 --> 00:03:45.370
No!

00:03:45.370 --> 00:03:47.120
Scarred! No!

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:49.580
Honestly, who does this man think he is?!

00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:52.250
You're a big Gracula, aren't you?

00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:53.760
I am not!

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:57.300
Believe it or not, I, the great man, Milton, am a glorious crow! A crow!

00:03:57.300 --> 00:03:58.800
Here you go, Sir Grac.

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:00.340
It's barbequed meat.

00:04:00.550 --> 00:04:04.850
No. Do not think that I would take meat from an enemy's hand...

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:06.560
This is delicious!

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:07.350
Where is this meat from?

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:09.440
It's probably a Mikawa fowl.

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:10.610
No!

00:04:10.610 --> 00:04:13.900
This is practically cannibalism, but it's so good!

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:14.730
Delicious fowl!

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:17.650
If I could follow the Testament

00:04:17.650 --> 00:04:20.070
and save those who shake the times...

00:04:20.530 --> 00:04:22.410
I'm referring to what you mentioned a second ago.

00:04:23.030 --> 00:04:27.160
Even if the event only gets brief mention in the records of history,

00:04:27.910 --> 00:04:31.500
merely the honor of being a part of that history is good enough for me.

00:04:34.050 --> 00:04:35.420
I, Milton, am hen-pecking at fowl.

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:36.210
What's this?

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:38.090
An Eight-Span Crow?

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:41.180
I-I am not an Eight-Span Crow!

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:43.550
I'm Grac the Gracula!

00:04:43.550 --> 00:04:45.890
Hanami, go contact Father!

00:04:45.890 --> 00:04:49.020
Tell him that an Eight-Span Crow is eating BBQ in England.

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:51.770
He's been tainted, so we need to cleanse him.

00:04:52.730 --> 00:04:54.860
Please, anything but that!

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:57.280
An Eight-Span Crow?

00:04:57.280 --> 00:04:58.150
Right.

00:04:58.150 --> 00:05:01.950
It's a Kumano-style animal spirit mouse affiliated with a shrine.

00:05:01.950 --> 00:05:04.580
It should be doing volunteer work at some shrine.

00:05:04.580 --> 00:05:05.620
Nice and slow...

00:05:05.620 --> 00:05:06.580
Ah, hey!
Nice and slow...

00:05:06.580 --> 00:05:08.410
Secret Move: A Crow in the Moonless Night!

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:13.000
Clap!

00:05:16.170 --> 00:05:20.090
Sheesh! I'm amazed he has been able to survive on his own.

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:24.890
Judge. It's because England doesn't have as many strange beings as the Far East.

00:05:24.890 --> 00:05:26.350
I see...

00:05:26.350 --> 00:05:28.100
Dude in the cloak!

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:30.350
Since you're familiar with Earth pulse interactions,

00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:32.190
have you heard of this?

00:05:32.190 --> 00:05:33.480
Nikyou Crests.

00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:34.610
Nikyou Crests?

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:36.610
He means this.

00:05:37.690 --> 00:05:41.780
They tend to appear when someone is spirited away and becomes a "Lost One".

00:05:44.660 --> 00:05:47.660
Wouldn't you know it, England is investigating that as well.

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:49.290
<i>"Wouldn't you know it"?</i>

00:05:49.290 --> 00:05:51.580
If you're investigating it, where did it happen?

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:54.630
Well...

00:05:54.630 --> 00:05:57.710
If you form friendly relations with those on the top level,

00:05:57.710 --> 00:06:00.920
you should ask them about a place called "Avalon".

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:02.340
Avalon?

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:05.430
I am afraid that I cannot say much beyond that

00:06:05.430 --> 00:06:06.720
as I myself am an outsider.

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:09.310
Judge.

00:06:09.310 --> 00:06:12.640
Just learning that England has information on it is helpful.

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:13.690
It's done.

00:06:14.190 --> 00:06:15.230
A kobold?!

00:06:15.230 --> 00:06:16.440
Yeah!

00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:18.860
He helped make the hot spring bathhouse.

00:06:22.860 --> 00:06:24.360
I'll take it.

00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:26.740
Got it.

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:28.780
In that case, Tenzo and the dude in the cloak,

00:06:28.780 --> 00:06:30.750
I'll give ya first dibs on the bath, so have at it!

00:06:31.540 --> 00:06:33.790
There might be some issues with the construction,

00:06:33.790 --> 00:06:35.250
so it'll also serve as a test run.

00:06:35.250 --> 00:06:37.710
B-But, I couldn't possibly...

00:06:37.710 --> 00:06:39.920
What's keeping you? Get going already!

00:06:43.630 --> 00:06:46.300
B-Be sure not to peep!

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:49.010
Who would want to peep on you in the bath?

00:06:51.430 --> 00:06:53.020
Those two...

00:06:53.020 --> 00:06:54.890
...are acting suspicious.

00:06:56.770 --> 00:07:00.980
Adele easily blurted out something I don't even want to think about...

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:04.610
Well, I guess it's cool since England's Protestant and all.

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:07.160
Come to think of it...

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:10.790
Could you tell me a bit more about sex?

00:07:10.790 --> 00:07:13.200
Wh-What did you just say?!

00:07:13.660 --> 00:07:16.870
When I brought it up with Miriam just like Naruze taught me,

00:07:16.870 --> 00:07:18.630
she got really angry.

00:07:18.630 --> 00:07:21.550
I think I must have misunderstood what you said.

00:07:21.550 --> 00:07:25.380
So I'd like you to explain it again so I can straighten things out.

00:07:26.930 --> 00:07:30.350
Th-There is only so much I could teach you!

00:07:30.350 --> 00:07:31.310
So, uh...

00:07:31.310 --> 00:07:32.470
Not me.

00:07:33.060 --> 00:07:34.020
Masazumi!

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:36.140
<i>Why did she toss the ball to me?!</i>

00:07:37.020 --> 00:07:39.360
I would like you to explain it to me as well.

00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:41.070
<i>Now she wants to know!</i>

00:07:41.070 --> 00:07:43.190
As I do not know what that word means,

00:07:43.190 --> 00:07:44.440
I would appreciate an explanation.

00:07:44.440 --> 00:07:46.320
<i>Not you, too!</i>

00:07:47.780 --> 00:07:50.950
Well, lift up and thrust...

00:07:50.950 --> 00:07:53.200
Huh? What was that, Seijun?

00:07:54.580 --> 00:07:59.790
I-It's a proper way to mutually deepen your bonds with another.

00:07:59.790 --> 00:08:00.290
Right...

00:08:00.290 --> 00:08:01.670
That's all it is!

00:08:01.670 --> 00:08:03.300
I see.

00:08:09.140 --> 00:08:09.930
Um...

00:08:09.930 --> 00:08:11.890
Wh-What is it?

00:08:11.890 --> 00:08:15.520
I looked over the floor and tub and there didn't seem to be any problems.

00:08:15.520 --> 00:08:17.140
I-Is that right?

00:08:17.140 --> 00:08:19.560
Uh, Master Tenzo?

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:20.770
What is it?

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:25.860
I don't mind, so please come join me.

00:08:27.490 --> 00:08:29.200
You don't want to bathe with me?

00:08:29.200 --> 00:08:30.070
Hardly!

00:08:30.360 --> 00:08:32.990
Then feel free to come in.

00:08:35.580 --> 00:08:38.290
Listen, after the party on the first day of the festival,

00:08:38.290 --> 00:08:40.290
we'll have a meeting with England.

00:08:40.290 --> 00:08:42.960
That is where we'll decide Musashi's next course of action.

00:08:42.960 --> 00:08:46.840
Aoi, please decide where you want to take things by then.

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:50.890
And if I can't make up my mind?

00:08:50.890 --> 00:08:52.260
In that case,

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:54.890
I'll take full responsibility and decide for you.

00:08:54.890 --> 00:08:58.350
It's just, I don't want to do that if I don't have to, so...

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:02.610
I know!

00:09:03.270 --> 00:09:05.270
Let's go on a date, Horizon!

00:09:06.400 --> 00:09:09.950
Wh-Why do you want to go on a date with Horizon now?

00:09:10.400 --> 00:09:13.370
There's a bunch of stuff I want to discuss with Horizon.

00:09:13.870 --> 00:09:16.040
What do you want to discuss?

00:09:16.040 --> 00:09:17.410
So like, Horizon,

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:19.710
you aren't interested in emotions, are you?

00:09:20.460 --> 00:09:24.290
Bluntly put, I feel they are unnecessary.

00:09:27.170 --> 00:09:28.630
<i>My king...!</i>

00:09:28.630 --> 00:09:30.550
Mitotsudaira!

00:09:30.550 --> 00:09:32.430
Care for some fried rice?

00:09:35.470 --> 00:09:37.850
Well, I guess that's only normal!

00:09:38.140 --> 00:09:39.730
<i>Thank goodness.</i>

00:09:40.270 --> 00:09:42.980
But I've decided to get them back.

00:09:43.310 --> 00:09:45.150
I've been plotting to somehow

00:09:45.150 --> 00:09:47.400
gather up all eight Armaments of Deadly Sins

00:09:47.400 --> 00:09:50.820
and hold a memorial service in your honor since before you came back.

00:09:50.820 --> 00:09:54.570
So you did not need me to begin with, did you?

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:56.160
That's not true!

00:09:56.450 --> 00:09:58.700
Do you need me as an excuse

00:09:58.700 --> 00:10:00.540
to retrieve these emotions?

00:10:00.540 --> 00:10:02.330
I said you've got it wrong!

00:10:02.330 --> 00:10:04.790
Then please do not retrieve them.

00:10:04.790 --> 00:10:07.710
Otherwise people will fight

00:10:07.710 --> 00:10:09.510
and get hurt because of me.

00:10:11.470 --> 00:10:15.090
You do not truly need me, do you?

00:10:19.060 --> 00:10:20.390
<i>This means...</i>

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:22.980
<i>The concept that she does not need herself</i>

00:10:22.980 --> 00:10:25.600
<i>comes from her ability as an automated doll to make the best decision.</i>

00:10:26.360 --> 00:10:29.530
<i>But now that she has Lypē Katarripsi,</i>

00:10:29.530 --> 00:10:31.780
<i>Horizon knows what it means to feel sad.</i>

00:10:33.650 --> 00:10:37.410
I do not need what I do not need.

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:41.330
Chancellor!

00:10:41.330 --> 00:10:43.080
Why don't you do something?

00:10:50.090 --> 00:10:51.340
What is it?

00:10:52.010 --> 00:10:53.340
Console the weeping,

00:10:53.340 --> 00:10:54.590
while catching a good look at

00:10:54.590 --> 00:10:56.140
the hefty cleavage.

00:10:59.260 --> 00:11:01.520
Serving justice by fighting off perversity.

00:11:01.520 --> 00:11:03.310
The ground's so close!

00:11:03.310 --> 00:11:05.850
N-Nice answer to my poem, Horizon!

00:11:06.980 --> 00:11:08.610
Let's go on a date, Horizon.

00:11:08.610 --> 00:11:10.610
Go on a date with me, see a bunch of stuff,

00:11:10.610 --> 00:11:12.230
pig out and have fun goofing off!

00:11:12.230 --> 00:11:15.740
Let's test to see if you develop any interest in emotions.

00:11:16.450 --> 00:11:18.450
What would happen after this test is over?

00:11:18.910 --> 00:11:22.450
If you feel like it, we could take back the Armaments of Deadly Sins together!

00:11:22.450 --> 00:11:24.370
That is a dangerous idea.

00:11:24.370 --> 00:11:28.580
Are you suggesting I start a world war if I decide I want my emotions back?

00:11:28.580 --> 00:11:32.210
Hey, now! World domination is my job.

00:11:32.210 --> 00:11:35.420
You're parallel to me, so think up something else.

00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:37.050
Let's start off by having that date

00:11:37.050 --> 00:11:38.340
so you can chew on that, too!

00:11:38.340 --> 00:11:40.970
You intend to take your doll outside to play?

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:41.680
Nope!

00:11:42.430 --> 00:11:44.850
I'm going to hold your hand and go out with you.

00:11:47.350 --> 00:11:48.770
Judge.

00:11:48.770 --> 00:11:52.360
I don't know what to think of deciding Musashi's affairs over a date,

00:11:52.360 --> 00:11:55.110
but it's worth a shot if the heir of the Far East

00:11:55.110 --> 00:11:56.530
gives her consent.

00:11:59.530 --> 00:12:01.830
As such, let's draw this meeting to a close.

00:12:02.870 --> 00:12:04.040
Ummm...

00:12:04.950 --> 00:12:07.410
I just got word, but...

00:12:07.410 --> 00:12:10.210
Apparently Lypē Katarripsi has gone missing.

00:12:11.000 --> 00:12:11.960
Huh?

00:12:17.510 --> 00:12:19.890
I'm not sure what to make of this situation.

00:12:21.050 --> 00:12:22.930
My body is so covered in scars

00:12:22.930 --> 00:12:25.060
that you wouldn't enjoy what you saw if you looked.

00:12:25.350 --> 00:12:26.730
That's not—

00:12:27.810 --> 00:12:29.140
That's not true...

00:12:29.140 --> 00:12:30.270
As far as I can tell,

00:12:30.270 --> 00:12:33.650
the scars only cover your front half.

00:12:33.650 --> 00:12:35.150
I imagine you have always

00:12:35.150 --> 00:12:37.950
faced your opponents head on.

00:12:39.030 --> 00:12:43.950
I gave myself these scars because I wanted to.

00:12:43.950 --> 00:12:45.910
I didn't care if I died...

00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:48.750
Then I think you should continue to do so

00:12:48.750 --> 00:12:50.290
until you feel satisfied.

00:12:50.790 --> 00:12:53.960
But it would seem to me that you have already done enough.

00:12:53.960 --> 00:12:54.920
That is because...

00:12:55.460 --> 00:12:56.380
Because what?

00:12:57.130 --> 00:12:59.430
Because it is evident that you are

00:12:59.430 --> 00:13:00.720
a truly honorable individual.

00:13:00.720 --> 00:13:04.010
There is no need to injure yourself further.

00:13:08.980 --> 00:13:10.060
Master Scarred?

00:13:10.060 --> 00:13:11.850
Did I say something wrong?

00:13:16.860 --> 00:13:18.990
I'll get out first.

00:13:26.040 --> 00:13:28.000
<i>A piece of the cargo ship's outer hull?</i>

00:13:31.210 --> 00:13:33.040
<i>An anti-spell coating?</i>

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:34.670
<i>It's a spell repellent type.</i>

00:13:36.960 --> 00:13:39.840
<i>If I had used my spell back there...</i>

00:13:39.840 --> 00:13:42.090
<i>...it would have sent the cargo ship flying</i>

00:13:42.090 --> 00:13:44.890
<i>while simultaneously repelling that power back at the kids.</i>

00:13:45.430 --> 00:13:46.970
<i>That's why this man...</i>

00:13:51.190 --> 00:13:52.390
Master Tenzo...

00:13:55.610 --> 00:13:56.820
<i>Boobs!</i>

00:13:57.150 --> 00:13:58.610
Wh-Wh-Wh-Wha...?

00:13:58.610 --> 00:14:00.780
This is the injury you got back there.

00:14:00.780 --> 00:14:02.570
May I heal it for you?

00:14:03.320 --> 00:14:05.410
M-May I ask that of you?

00:14:05.410 --> 00:14:06.580
Judge.

00:14:10.250 --> 00:14:12.160
Please don't turn back.

00:14:12.160 --> 00:14:14.250
It would make the spell miss the wound.

00:14:15.630 --> 00:14:16.750
Judge.

00:14:20.210 --> 00:14:22.010
What a great night!

00:14:24.510 --> 00:14:26.850
We searched high and low,

00:14:26.850 --> 00:14:28.930
but in the end, we failed to find

00:14:28.930 --> 00:14:30.850
Horizon's Armament of Deadly Sins.

00:14:30.850 --> 00:14:33.890
The mothership is mighty big and all.

00:14:33.890 --> 00:14:37.360
W-We used a spell t-to search for it,

00:14:37.360 --> 00:14:39.480
so we know it's inside the ship.

00:14:39.480 --> 00:14:41.860
Wouldn't it be something if Horizon was half asleep

00:14:41.860 --> 00:14:44.450
when she put it somewhere and forgot where she left it?

00:14:44.450 --> 00:14:45.200
Indeed.

00:14:45.910 --> 00:14:48.780
The search for Lypē Katarripsi will continue on.

00:14:50.330 --> 00:14:53.120
Now then, shall we get started?

00:14:53.120 --> 00:14:55.080
Are we seriously doing this?

00:14:55.080 --> 00:14:57.920
Isn't it troublesome not having a mouse around?

00:14:59.250 --> 00:15:03.090
First I am going to temporarily cancel your contract with Mikawa.

00:15:03.090 --> 00:15:05.180
What will happen to the contract with my homeland's guardian deity?

00:15:05.180 --> 00:15:08.010
Since we're allied with Mikawa's guardian deity,

00:15:08.010 --> 00:15:09.930
you can keep your old contract.

00:15:09.930 --> 00:15:14.350
But your contract is still the same as when you were born and lacks a portable form,

00:15:14.350 --> 00:15:15.850
so it offers weak protection.

00:15:15.850 --> 00:15:16.810
Really?

00:15:17.310 --> 00:15:20.520
I think that might be why you were always about to starve to death.

00:15:20.820 --> 00:15:25.070
I'll add sun block and skin protection as free bonus features.

00:15:25.070 --> 00:15:26.860
I don't really need those...

00:15:26.860 --> 00:15:28.200
Let's see...

00:15:28.200 --> 00:15:29.830
Before you make a contract with a mouse,

00:15:29.830 --> 00:15:32.740
you can make a personal contract with the deity you'd like to worship.

00:15:32.740 --> 00:15:33.450
Would you like to do that?

00:15:35.410 --> 00:15:38.130
Could I make that contract some other time?

00:15:38.130 --> 00:15:40.920
Not a problem, as long as you come to me for the service.

00:15:42.420 --> 00:15:44.670
A naked Asama told Masazumi,

00:15:44.670 --> 00:15:46.260
"As long as you come to me for the service."

00:15:47.180 --> 00:15:48.970
Sweet! Look forward to the next chapter!

00:15:48.970 --> 00:15:52.310
Gacchan, you've got enough material to last you another five years!

00:15:53.600 --> 00:15:58.150
You'll need a special mouse when you eventually make a personal contract,

00:15:58.150 --> 00:16:01.110
so why don't you get a multipurpose mouse for now?

00:16:01.110 --> 00:16:04.190
Even though they're multipurpose, they're pretty pricey.

00:16:04.190 --> 00:16:05.610
Isn't there some way to cut the price?

00:16:06.110 --> 00:16:08.660
Then let's use a contract by blessing.

00:16:09.200 --> 00:16:10.870
A contract by blessing?

00:16:10.870 --> 00:16:14.160
Yeah. Your mouse is selected at random.

00:16:14.160 --> 00:16:16.120
Is that wise?

00:16:16.540 --> 00:16:21.380
Normally people get one of the numerous dog, rat, fox or bird mice.

00:16:21.380 --> 00:16:24.960
Sometimes people get expensive mice, so it's a good deal.

00:16:29.180 --> 00:16:30.010
Clap!

00:16:34.060 --> 00:16:36.100
What's this? Oh, my!

00:16:36.100 --> 00:16:38.020
What's with that exclamation, Asama?

00:16:38.020 --> 00:16:39.440
So here's a question for you:

00:16:39.440 --> 00:16:41.150
What mouse did you get?

00:16:41.150 --> 00:16:42.440
How would I know?!

00:16:42.980 --> 00:16:44.900
Then here's a hint: It's an animal.

00:16:46.860 --> 00:16:47.650
A fox!

00:16:47.650 --> 00:16:51.200
Wrong! Next hint: Its name starts with a vowel!

00:16:51.200 --> 00:16:52.990
<i>A vowel...?</i>

00:16:52.990 --> 00:16:56.120
<i>"An," "E"... "Eagle. An eagle?</i>

00:16:56.620 --> 00:16:58.540
<i>An eagle, huh? I like that.</i>

00:16:58.540 --> 00:17:01.000
Okay, Asama! Open her up!

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:01.750
Got it.

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:07.460
Tada! It's an anteater!

00:17:07.460 --> 00:17:08.720
What type of trickery is this?!

00:17:09.090 --> 00:17:13.180
Lately Izumo has been conducting business in Kyushu and the New World, so...

00:17:13.180 --> 00:17:16.100
Yeah, but... an anteater?

00:17:17.770 --> 00:17:21.020
It looks like it's a little too young.

00:17:21.020 --> 00:17:22.150
What should we do?

00:17:22.150 --> 00:17:23.900
Would you like a different mouse?

00:17:23.900 --> 00:17:25.150
Well...

00:17:25.860 --> 00:17:29.610
It's probably just scared because it doesn't know much about the outside world.

00:17:32.360 --> 00:17:33.490
It's okay.

00:17:33.490 --> 00:17:34.830
Are you sure?

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:36.080
Judge!

00:17:37.370 --> 00:17:39.750
Now even Masazumi has a kid.

00:17:39.750 --> 00:17:41.580
How wonderful...

00:17:41.580 --> 00:17:44.290
Huh? Suzu?! H-Hey!

00:17:45.170 --> 00:17:46.500
You're even bigger than me!

00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:48.590
She can use her boobs as hooks on my arms!

00:17:48.590 --> 00:17:50.170
D-Dammit!

00:17:50.170 --> 00:17:51.300
Adele.

00:17:51.300 --> 00:17:52.590
Y-Yes?

00:17:53.300 --> 00:17:54.800
No, no.

00:17:54.800 --> 00:17:57.100
Girls shouldn't use dirty words like that.

00:17:57.100 --> 00:17:58.180
Right...

00:18:00.980 --> 00:18:02.310
Listen, Bell.

00:18:02.310 --> 00:18:03.940
If they say something you don't like,

00:18:03.940 --> 00:18:06.400
just cough to slide right past it.

00:18:06.400 --> 00:18:08.860
Will that be okay?

00:18:08.860 --> 00:18:09.820
You bet!

00:18:09.820 --> 00:18:11.360
That's how diplomacy works!

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:13.660
Is she really going to be okay?

00:18:13.660 --> 00:18:14.700
Probably...

00:18:22.160 --> 00:18:25.580
Now then, let's start preparing to bring in the money!

00:18:25.580 --> 00:18:26.790
Yeah...

00:18:45.100 --> 00:18:48.980
As the Vice-President of Musashi Ariadust Academy,

00:18:48.980 --> 00:18:52.490
I, Honda Masazumi, hereby declare the start of

00:18:52.490 --> 00:18:55.410
the joint spring festival between Musashi and England!

00:19:02.910 --> 00:19:05.120
Well, we'll be back in a bit.

00:19:05.120 --> 00:19:08.170
Don't forget we have a meeting with England this evening.

00:19:08.460 --> 00:19:10.050
I'll remember!

00:19:10.050 --> 00:19:11.510
Let's go, Horizon.

00:19:11.510 --> 00:19:12.260
Judge.

00:19:17.510 --> 00:19:18.640
I love you!

00:19:30.860 --> 00:19:32.730
<i>Thomas Shakespeare?!</i>

00:19:33.320 --> 00:19:35.030
Is the spot next to you open?

00:19:51.380 --> 00:19:52.670
Now go.

00:19:53.760 --> 00:19:55.090
I got it!

00:19:57.050 --> 00:19:58.760
Was that some sort of ceremony?

00:19:59.260 --> 00:20:00.970
It's simple, Asama.

00:20:00.970 --> 00:20:02.470
I told him that he wasn't posing as a gentleman,

00:20:02.470 --> 00:20:06.940
but there is nothing wrong with an unpolished child reaching out to me.

00:20:06.940 --> 00:20:08.310
Uh-huh...

00:20:08.310 --> 00:20:09.980
More importantly, Mitotsudaira,

00:20:09.980 --> 00:20:12.020
can you trail my foolish brother?

00:20:17.110 --> 00:20:19.530
Judge, that isn't a problem.

00:20:19.530 --> 00:20:22.030
His hair smells just like yours.

00:20:22.030 --> 00:20:26.080
Sometimes I think that Mitotsudaira is pretty amazing.

00:20:28.870 --> 00:20:30.670
Tres España!

00:20:39.130 --> 00:20:39.930
Can you see that?

00:20:40.470 --> 00:20:41.220
Tes.

00:20:43.010 --> 00:20:44.180
Isn't that...?

00:20:44.180 --> 00:20:45.060
Judge.

00:20:45.060 --> 00:20:47.600
It is the bell in the Tower of London's chapel.

00:20:47.600 --> 00:20:49.350
It is a sign that Double Bloody Mary,

00:20:49.940 --> 00:20:52.310
Mary Stuart, will show herself.

00:20:55.110 --> 00:20:58.700
Master Tenzo, what do you think of her execution?

00:21:00.410 --> 00:21:04.490
She will be executed for a failed attempt on Queen Elizabeth's life.

00:21:04.490 --> 00:21:10.330
And since she is Catholic, her execution will be what triggers the Anglo-Spanish Armada Battle.

00:21:10.620 --> 00:21:13.500
She only has one week left.

00:21:13.500 --> 00:21:15.420
Her execution will be held

00:21:15.420 --> 00:21:17.420
when this festival draws to an end.

00:21:18.050 --> 00:21:19.800
I know...

00:21:19.800 --> 00:21:23.640
But even though it's called an execution, they won't really take her life.

00:21:23.640 --> 00:21:26.220
Don't they have something else prepared for her?

00:21:26.220 --> 00:21:30.310
Judge. Mary Stuart will be "saved".

00:21:30.770 --> 00:21:32.810
I'm glad to hear it.

00:21:33.940 --> 00:21:34.940
My apologies!

00:21:34.940 --> 00:21:36.320
I spoke out of line.

00:21:36.320 --> 00:21:38.650
No, it's okay.

00:21:40.280 --> 00:21:41.320
What are you doing here?

00:21:41.320 --> 00:21:43.870
Don't look this way.

00:21:44.830 --> 00:21:46.950
Yes, stay just like that.

00:21:46.950 --> 00:21:49.410
A bunch of stuff is about to start happening,

00:21:49.410 --> 00:21:53.250
but you can't do anything about it since you're my Macbeth.

00:21:59.920 --> 00:22:01.380
There is a change in the air.

00:22:01.800 --> 00:22:03.840
Mary isn't there anymore, huh?

00:22:03.840 --> 00:22:06.560
I can sense a powerful aura in the city.

00:22:06.560 --> 00:22:08.680
In fact, I sense several...

00:22:09.720 --> 00:22:10.980
This is strange.

00:22:11.310 --> 00:22:14.810
Why don't we go to the top level, Master Tenzo?

00:22:15.230 --> 00:22:19.780
I shall take you to where I know someone became a Lost Noble.

00:22:20.820 --> 00:22:22.450
What have you started?!

00:22:22.450 --> 00:22:24.240
I prepared the stage.

00:22:26.240 --> 00:22:29.200
I prepared the comedy, "Much Ado About Nothing".

00:22:42.340 --> 00:22:43.340
The curtain has risen,

00:22:45.720 --> 00:22:46.260
gentlemen.
